{
  "rationale": "Each test implements the plan's intent while staying within the specification. Where the plan would need the submission's code or a full solution, I used a direct check only on small n (test_small_brute). I strengthened test_output_format to include newline handling, and weakened test_min_leaves to only assert when leaves are less than half n (since spec implies leaves ≥ ceil((n+1)/2) for any such tree). I omitted bounds that could be false for some valid inputs (like test_sum_lower_bound) because the spec does not guarantee them. Instead I used only necessary conditions derived from tree properties: internal nodes ≥2 children implies no size 2, root size = n, leaves count bound, etc. All tests run fast on given inputs (n ≤ 24).",
